# Java 25 — the AMBIENT JVM: what launches sbt, and so what compiles
# everything (in-process dotc). Moved from 21 by java-gatherers
# (2026-09-23, operator): okay-java bridges `java.util.stream.Gatherer`
# (JDK 24+), and dotc sees only the class library of the JVM it runs
# in — no `-release` can grant a newer API to an older compiler.
#
# What compiling on 21 guaranteed by accident is now asked for by
# flag: every Scala 3 module carries `-java-output-version` 17 or 21
# (build.sbt, `jdkFloor`), so the compiler still refuses an API newer
# than the module's floor; bytecode stays major 61 on 17-floor modules,
# as it always was. See specs/java-gatherers.md.
#
# On JDK 24+ the Security Manager is gone (JEP 486) and with it
# Subject.getSubject, which Hadoop's UserGroupInformation calls on
# every job Spark runs. That is a RUNTIME matter and does not touch
# compiling: Spark 4.2.0's own confirmed range is 17/21/25
# (spark-jdk25-guard-fix), and okaySpark's build.sbt settings pin its
# Test/run to 25 regardless of what this file says.
#
# `sdk env install` here, or `sdk env` in a shell that already has it.
java=25.0.4.1-tem

# TEST/RUN — a SEPARATE knob (jdk26-default-runtime, 2026-09-19):
# build.sbt defaults every module's forked Test/run to the newest GA
# JDK this project has actually verified end to end
# (~/.sdkman/candidates/java/26.0.2.1-tem — 27 is not GA at this date),
# not the ambient one above. Compiling is the ambient 25; a released
# service, a `sbt run`, and every test suite but okaySpark's now
# execute on 26 by default. See specs/jdk-compatibility.md.
